---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import { loadSizes } from '../data/business';
---

<Layout
  title="How Junk Removal Pricing Works"
  description="Single-item pickup starts at $125 in Lancaster County. See what affects the final junk removal price and request a quote for larger loads."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Pricing', url: '/pricing' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">KNOW WHAT GOES INTO THE COST</p>
      <h1>
        A clear estimate.
        <br />A simpler decision.
      </h1>
      <p>
        No two piles are quite the same. The best place to start is with what
        you have and where it needs to come from.
      </p>
      <CTA />
    </section>
    <section class="callout pricing-starting-price" aria-labelledby="starting-price">
      <p class="eyebrow">A PLACE TO START</p>
      <h2 id="starting-price">Single-Item Pickup — Starting at $125</h2>
      <p>
        Have one bulky item you need gone? Single-item pickups start at $125,
        including loading, hauling, and standard disposal. This is a starting
        price, not a promise that every item costs exactly $125. Final pricing
        is confirmed with you before we load anything.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="content-grid page-content">
      <div>
        <h2>Four things shape the estimate.</h2>
        <ol class="plain-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Volume.</strong> How much room the items take up in a load.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Materials and weight.</strong> Heavy items, unusual
            materials, and special handling can affect the work and disposal
            requirements.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Access and distance.</strong> Stairs, difficult access,
            distance to the truck or service location, and disassembly can
            affect the work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Disposal requirements.</strong> The type of material
            determines which handling options are appropriate.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <h2>Photos are a useful starting point.</h2>
        <p>
          Take a wide photo of the items together, then another of the access
          route. Mention anything not visible, such as upstairs items or an
          appliance connection. An on-site look may be needed to confirm the
          scope.
        </p>
        <h2>For larger loads, request a quote.</h2>
        <p>
          Larger projects are priced from their actual scope. Amount or volume,
          weight, stairs, difficult access, distance, special handling, disposal
          requirements, and certain items with additional disposal fees can all
          affect the estimate. Request a quote and include photos if helpful.
        </p>
        <div class="load-sizes">
          {loadSizes.map((s) => (
            <span>{s}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p>
          These amount choices help describe a project; they are not published
          load rates or guaranteed truck capacities. Final pricing is confirmed
          before loading begins.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="callout">
        <h2>Help us see the whole picture.</h2>
        <p>
          Include your item list, ZIP, photos if you have them, and any stairs
          or access limitations. Tell us your timing, too.
        </p>
        <p>
          There’s no need to guess how much truck space you’ll need. We’ll
          discuss the estimate before loading anything.
        </p>
        <CTA />
      </aside>
    </section>
    <div class="section">
      <FinalCTA />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
